  "description": "Upgrade this application to a newer release of the template it was generated from, which is how this application moves to a newer NocoBase version. Users rarely think in terms of templates, so use it whenever the user asks to upgrade or update NocoBase, the NocoBase core, kernel or framework version, or the @nocobase packages as a whole — for example \"upgrade NocoBase\", \"update the NocoBase core version\", \"move to the latest NocoBase release\", \"升级 NocoBase\", \"升级 NocoBase 内核版本\", \"更新 NocoBase 到最新版\" — as well as when they ask to upgrade the template, pull in template changes, move to a newer template version, or reconcile the application with upstream. Do not use for ordinary feature development, for upgrading a single dependency, or for upgrading an already deployed build on a server, which the app installer handles.",
